step1-
first we want to create virtual environment
-------------------------------------------
python -m venv djven





step2-
Activate virtual environment
---------------------------
djvenv\scripts\activate





----open powershell as admin ----SetExecutionPolicy remotesigned--y







step-3
install django
--------------
pip install Django










step-4

start a project in django
------------------------

django-admin startproject django_tutorial









step-5
enter the project folder
----------------------------
cd django_tutorial










step-6
create an app(component) into the project
------------------------------
python manage.py startapp home



step-7
how to run a backend server
-------------------
python manage.py runserver









step-8
mounting the home to project
----------------------------
select djangoproject
click settings.py---select installed apps---then type 'home',

step-9
MVT Design pattern (python followed this pattern )
model.view.templete
-------------------------------------------------
url mapping 
-----------
1-- Create a urls.py file in home app
2-- djangoproject------------url.py--------
    path(".include"("home.urls")),

//this home page will come first while run 


---------------------------------------------------
App URLS first empty path url define 
____________________________________
from django.urls import path.include
from .import views

urlpatterns = [
    path(",views.home, name = 'home'),


]


--------------------------------------------------
--define first view.in views.py
-home function

from django.http import HttpResponse

def home(request):
    return HttpResponse("HOME page is working")

def about(request):
    return HttpResponse("About page is working") 



then go to view.py and create functions like index,about,etc..

from django.shortcuts import render
from django.http import HttpResponse

def home(request):
    return render(request, 'home.html')

def about(request):
    return render(request, 'about.html')   


step-10

django templates  ------which means html file
--------------------------------------------------

--create a templates folder and
--- create html file then...
-- add this into settings.py's in project folder.
eg:
TEMPLATES = 
   
 -----------  'DIRS': ['templates'],------------------------
       
------------------------------------------------------------------------
--then add this into views.py 

def index(request):
    return render(request, 'index.html')

-----------------------


step-12

Template inheritance
---------------------

create base.html file(skelton file)


blocks : {% block content%} {% endblock %}   ------add this in changes occurring fields.(title,body,..etc) 

Inheritance :{% extends "base.html" %}       ------- using extends every html pages can Inherit base.html file 



------------------------------------------




step-13

how to activate  navbar in base html
---------------------
1-first we have to give the name ='home'  --- in app(home)------urls.py

eg--- path('',views.index,name='home'),
    path('about',views.about,name='about'),
    path('booking',views.booking,name='booking'),


2-second goto base.html and replace href="#"   to -----  {% url 'home'%}
-----------------------
eg-----  <a class="nav-link text-white" href="{% url 'home'%}">Home </a>
            </li>
            <li class="nav-item">
              <a class="nav-link text-white" href="{% url 'about'%}">About</a>
            </li>
            <li class="nav-item">
              <a class="nav-link text-white" href="{% url 'booking'%}">Booking</a>
            </li>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------